---
import type { ImageMetadata } from 'astro';

import type { TranscriptAuthor } from '@/landing/transcript';

import MessageCard from '@/components/landing/message-card.astro';
import Layout from '@/components/layout.astro';

import { POSTURES, REFUSALS } from '@/landing/argument';
import { TRANSCRIPT } from '@/landing/transcript';

import clara from '@/assets/clara.png';
import orchestrator from '@/assets/orchestrator.png';
import theo from '@/assets/theo.png';

const AVATARS: { [K in TranscriptAuthor]: ImageMetadata } = { clara, orchestrator, theo };

const description =
  "Collegium runs LLM agents as members of your team's chat, handling email, research, and follow-through, with a human approving anything consequential.";
---

<Layout description={description} theme="user" title="Collegium">
  <div class="landing flex flex-1 flex-col">
    <header class="border-lp-border bg-lp-background/80 fixed inset-x-0 top-0 z-50 border-b backdrop-blur">
      <div class="mx-auto flex h-14 w-full max-w-3xl items-center gap-6 px-6">
        <a class="flex items-center gap-2.5 text-sm font-medium" href="/">
          <svg aria-hidden="true" class="size-5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 32 32">
            <path d="M21.5 11.6a7 7 0 1 0 0 8.8" stroke="currentColor" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-width="3"></path>
          </svg>
          Collegium
        </a>
        <nav class="text-lp-muted ml-auto flex items-center gap-5 text-sm">
          <a class="hover:text-lp-text transition-colors" href="/docs/getting-started/introduction">Docs</a>
          <a
            class="hover:text-lp-text transition-colors"
            href="https://github.com/joshunrau/collegium"
            rel="noreferrer"
            target="_blank">GitHub</a
          >
          <button
            aria-label="Toggle colour theme"
            class="hover:text-lp-text hover:border-lp-border rounded-md border border-transparent p-1.5 transition-colors"
            id="lp-theme-toggle"
            type="button"
          >
            <svg
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="size-4"
              fill="none"
              stroke="currentColor"
              stroke-width="1.6"
              viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            >
              <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle>
              <path d="M12 3a9 9 0 0 0 0 18Z" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"></path>
            </svg>
          </button>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main class="mx-auto flex w-full max-w-3xl flex-1 flex-col gap-24 px-6 pt-36 pb-28">
      <section class="flex flex-col items-start gap-6">
        <span class="text-lp-muted font-lp-mono text-xs tracking-widest uppercase">Collegium</span>
        <h1 class="font-lp-serif max-w-2xl text-4xl leading-[1.08] tracking-tight text-balance sm:text-5xl">
          The agent framework for the work you can't git revert
        </h1>
        <p class="text-lp-muted max-w-xl leading-relaxed sm:text-lg">
          Collegium agents are members of your team's chat, each with its own name, tools, and memory. They handle the
          work that isn't writing software, like email, research, and follow-through.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a
            class="bg-lp-text text-lp-background rounded-lg px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium transition-opacity hover:opacity-90"
            href="/docs/getting-started/quickstart"
          >
            Quickstart
          </a>
          <a
            class="border-lp-border hover:bg-lp-surface rounded-lg border px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium transition-colors"
            href="https://github.com/joshunrau/collegium"
            rel="noreferrer"
            target="_blank"
          >
            GitHub
          </a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-8">
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
          <h2 class="text-lp-muted font-lp-mono text-xs tracking-widest uppercase">One job, end to end</h2>
          <p class="text-lp-muted max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
            An email arrives, Clara owns the reply, Theo digs up the facts, and a person approves the send. Everything
            below is a channel you could scroll.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
          {TRANSCRIPT.map((turn) => <MessageCard avatar={AVATARS[turn.author]} turn={turn} />)}
        </div>
        <p class="text-lp-muted max-w-2xl text-sm leading-relaxed">
          The announcement is deterministic code, not an agent deciding your mail matters. The approval shows the entire
          payload: every recipient, the full body, nothing summarized. And the send happens exactly once or not at all:
          an ambiguous outcome stops the turn rather than retrying your client's inbox.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-2">
        <h2 class="text-lp-muted font-lp-mono text-xs tracking-widest uppercase">What it commits to</h2>
        <ol class="flex flex-col">
          {
            POSTURES.map((posture, index) => (
              <li class="border-lp-border grid gap-x-8 gap-y-2 border-t py-7 sm:grid-cols-[3rem_1fr]">
                <span class="text-lp-muted font-lp-mono pt-1 text-xs">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
                <div class="flex max-w-2xl flex-col gap-2">
                  <h3 class="font-lp-serif text-xl tracking-tight">{posture.title}</h3>
                  <p class="text-lp-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">{posture.body}</p>
                </div>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section class="flex flex-col gap-6">
        <h2 class="font-lp-serif text-3xl tracking-tight">Why It's Built This Way</h2>
        <div class="flex max-w-2xl flex-col gap-4">
          <p class="text-lp-muted leading-relaxed">
            Most agent frameworks share one shape: give a model a shell and let it iterate unattended until the task
            looks done. That shape was built for writing software, where a failed attempt costs nothing and every change
            is reviewable as a diff before it ships.
          </p>
          <p class="text-lp-muted leading-relaxed">
            Business work is different. Actions are visible to clients and colleagues the moment they happen, many
            cannot be taken back, and nobody reviews them line by line afterward. So Collegium refuses four things
            autonomous frameworks celebrate, and each refusal is the point.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ul class="flex flex-col">
          {
            REFUSALS.map((refusal) => (
              <li class="border-lp-border grid gap-x-10 gap-y-5 border-t py-8 md:grid-cols-2">
                <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
                  <h3 class="font-lp-serif text-xl tracking-tight">{refusal.title}</h3>
                  <p class="text-lp-muted text-sm leading-relaxed">{refusal.what}</p>
                </div>
                <div class="border-lp-accent/50 flex flex-col gap-2 border-l pl-5">
                  <span class="text-lp-accent font-lp-mono text-xs tracking-widest uppercase">The cost</span>
                  <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed">{refusal.cost}</p>
                </div>
              </li>
            ))
          }
        </ul>
        <p class="max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
          And instead of autonomy, you get a system that runs your business logic as code. A procedure that matters is
          not a prompt instruction the model might skip on a bad day. It is a plugin: deterministic TypeScript you write
          once, review once, and grant to the agents that need it. It will not change under you.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script>
  const bind = () => {
    document.getElementById('lp-theme-toggle')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const dark = !document.documentElement.classList.contains('dark');
      document.documentElement.classList.toggle('dark', dark);
      document.documentElement.style.colorScheme = dark ? 'dark' : 'light';
      localStorage.setItem('collegium-theme', dark ? 'dark' : 'light');
    });
  };

  bind();
  document.addEventListener('astro:after-swap', bind);
</script>
